---
The **Export Leads** feature allows you to download your lead data from the system in a structured file format (CSV). This is useful for reporting, backups, data migration, and sharing information with external tools or teams.

## Overview

With Export Leads, you can:

- Download all leads or filtered data
- Create backups of your CRM data
- Analyze leads in external tools (e.g., Excel, Google Sheets)
- Share lead data with stakeholders

Exports are generated in **CSV format**, ensuring compatibility with most systems.

## Navigation

To access the export feature:

1. Go to **Leads**
1. Click the **+ (Plus icon)** next to the **Create Lead** button
1. Select **Export**
1. You will be redirected to:\
   **Settings → Data Management → Exports**

## Export Options

Depending on system configuration, you may have the following options:

### 3.1 Export All Leads

- Downloads all lead records in the system

### 3.2 Export Filtered Leads

- Export only selected leads based on filters such as:
  - Status
  - Lead Source
  - Owner
  - Date range

## Export Process

### Step 1: Open Export Section

- Navigate to **Exports** under Data Management

### Step 2: Select Data Type

- Choose **Leads** as the export category

### Step 3: Apply Filters (Optional)

- Narrow down the data if needed

### Step 4: Click Export

- Start the export process

## System Behavior

- Export runs in the background
- A file is generated in **CSV format**
- Processing time depends on data size

## Notification

After initiating export, you may see:

- **Notification Message:**
  - *“Export started. Your file will be available shortly.”*

Once ready:

- A download link may appear\
  **or**
- File may be available in the **Exports section**

## Download Export File

- Go to **Settings → Data Management → Exports**
- Locate your generated file
- Click **Download**

## Exported Data Fields

The exported CSV may include:

- First Name
- Last Name
- Email
- Phone
- Company Name
- Website
- Status
- Currency
- Lead Value
- Lead Source
- Last Interaction Date
- Lead Owner
- Country
- State
- City
- Zip Code
- Description
- Custom Fields (if configured)

## Use Cases

- Backup CRM data
- Share leads with marketing or sales teams
- Import data into another system
- Analyze lead performance externally
- Maintain offline records

## Best Practices

- Export data regularly for backup
- Use filters to export only relevant data
- Verify exported data before sharing
- Protect sensitive information when sharing files
- Keep exported files secure

## Troubleshooting

**Issue: Export file not**

- Wait for processing to complete
- Refresh the Exports page

**Issue: Missing data**

- Check applied filters
- Ensure all fields are mapped correctly

**Issue: File format issues**

- Open CSV in compatible tools like Excel or Google Sheets

## Notes

- Exported data reflects the state at the time of export
- Any changes made after export will not be included
- Custom fields are included if configured properly
